<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kathi people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kathis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kathi are a community of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a> peninsula in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, which is named after them. Pastoralists and warriors who are thought to have entered the region from the north in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a>, they founded several small states, including Jasdan, Jetpur and Bilkha. Their chiefs, known as Kathi Darbars, shared land among branches of the family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kathi-people.jpg" alt="Kathi people" width="320" height="511" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Baroda State · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathi_man.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
